.TH KAGI-VOLUME-IMAGE 1 "September 2026" "Kagi 0.38.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-image \- materialize a Kagi volume into a hypervisor image format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-volume-image
SOURCE OUTPUT FORMAT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses qemu-img-compatible conversion to create an independent qcow2, vmdk, vhdx, or other supported image from a Kagi block endpoint. The image is an export/copy; Kagi's native representation remains sparse object extents.
.SH SEE ALSO
kagi-volume-nbd(1), qemu-img(1)
